ar old duke of sussex would not be  attending as a preemptive safety measure  of course he had a very close  relationship with the duke of edinburgh  we understand the reason prince harry  won't be attending is because of  security and the situation as far as  harry is concerned is that he will not  have police protection over here and  therefore he doesn't feel safe bringing  his family over to britain but that  doesn't quite explain why he can't come  on his own a spokesperson for harry  shared that while the duke will not be  returning to the uk in late march he  hopes to visit his grandmother as soon  as possible we know that harry hasn't  seen the queen since last summer and of  course she's had a spate of ill health i  think most people are quite surprised  that he's not going to be coming over  here and so i think this is going to  further fuel talks of a continued rift  at the heart of the royal family and it  does raise questions i think about his  relationship with his grandmother once  so close and yet at that service of  thanksgiving prince harry won't be there  to support her or indeed to pay tribute  to his grandfather's life i think that's  probably a source of great sadness for  her majesty the queen  [Music]

